rk356x-npu-ocr - Rockchip RK356x (RK3566/RK3568) NPU PP-OCR engine for musl OpenWrt
====================================================================================

Supported hardware
------------------
  Supported:     RK3566 / RK3568  (RK356x family, RKNPU1 NPU generation)
  NOT supported: RK3588 / RK3576  (different NPU generation, needs different
                                  .rknn models and a different librknnrt build)

  Reasons the package is RK356x-only:
    * the engine is compiled with -DTARGET_SOC=rk356x;
    * the shipped .rknn models are RK3566/RK3568 (RKNPU1-compatible) blobs;
    * the bundled librknnrt.so is the RKNPU2 runtime matching the RK356x
      driver (v0.9.8, non-iommu mode).
  Loading these models on RK3588/RK3576 will fail.  For those SoCs build the
  RK3588 example of rknn_model_zoo with its RK3588 models instead.

What it installs
----------------
  /opt/ppocr/ppocr_demo              PP-OCR demo (glibc ELF)
  /opt/ppocr/models/ppocrv4_det.rknn PP-OCRv4 detection model (RK356x)
  /opt/ppocr/models/ppocrv4_rec.rknn PP-OCRv4 recognition model (RK356x)
  /opt/ppocr/keys/ppocr_keys_v1.txt  recognition dictionary
  /opt/ppocr/dict/ppocr_keys_v1.txt  same dictionary (compat path)
  /opt/ppocr/test.jpg                sample image for a smoke test
  /opt/rknpu/librknnrt.so            RKNN runtime 2.3.2 (Rockchip blob)
  /opt/glibc/                        glibc 2.35 loader + shared libraries
  /usr/bin/ppocr                     wrapper script
  /usr/bin/rk356x-npu-ocr            alias for the wrapper script

  The install paths under /opt (ppocr, rknpu, glibc) are deliberately kept
  unchanged so existing callers and the LuCI app keep working.

Usage
-----
  Single image:
      ppocr /opt/ppocr/test.jpg

  The wrapper runs the glibc engine through the bundled loader, equivalent to:
      /opt/glibc/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1 \
          --library-path /opt/glibc:/opt/rknpu \
          /opt/ppocr/ppocr_demo \
          /opt/ppocr/models/ppocrv4_det.rknn \
          /opt/ppocr/models/ppocrv4_rec.rknn <image>

  Multi-mode CLI (photo / screen / doc / table / video), when the CLI package or
  script is present at /opt/ppocr/ppocr:
      ppocr photo <image>
      ppocr screen <image>
      ppocr doc <image>
      ppocr table <image>
      ppocr video <clip>
  Override the CLI path with the PPOCR_CLI environment variable.

  The engine is quiet by default: it prints only the recognition result lines
  ("TEXT ...").  Pass --verbose (or -v) to restore the full diagnostics
  (model/tensor dumps, per-tile progress, IMAGE and TIMING lines).

Why a glibc bundle
------------------
The userland is musl, but librknnrt.so (Rockchip NPU runtime, proprietary
binary) and the OCR engine are glibc objects.  A small glibc runtime is bundled
under /opt/glibc so the engine can start on musl.  No musl libc/libstdcpp
dependency is needed.

License notes
-------------
  ppocr_demo, .rknn models, dictionary : Apache-2.0 (rknn_model_zoo, PaddleOCR)
  librknnrt.so                         : Rockchip proprietary, redistributable
  /opt/glibc/*                         : glibc (LGPL-2.1-or-later /
                                         GPL-2.0-or-later / GPL-3.0-GCC-exc)
